-- title:
--   Truncations of a flat unramified local extension are finite free
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring and $D$ a commutative local ring which is a $V$-algebra such that the structure map $V \to D$ is a local homomorphism and $D$ is flat as a $V$-module. Assume that the ideal of $D$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_V$ is exactly the maximal ideal of $D$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_V D = \mathfrak m_D$, and that the residue field $\kappa(D)$ is a finite (module-finite) extension of $\kappa(V)$. Then for every integer $m > 0$ the three following assertions hold simultaneously: the $(V/\mathfrak m_V^m)$-module $(V/\mathfrak m_V^m) \otimes_V D$ is module-finite; it is free; and its rank satisfies
--   $$\operatorname{finrank}_{V/\mathfrak m_V^m}\bigl((V/\mathfrak m_V^m) \otimes_V D\bigr) = \operatorname{finrank}_{\kappa(V)} \kappa(D),$$
--   the degree of the residue field extension. The conclusion is stated as a conjunction of the finiteness, freeness and rank statements for the given $m$; the base ring of the tensor product is $V$, while the module structure recorded in the conclusion is over the Artinian quotient $V/\mathfrak m_V^m$.
--
--   This is the levelwise commutative-algebra input for unramified flat local extensions: each truncation $D/\mathfrak m_V^m D$ of $D$ is finite free over $V/\mathfrak m_V^m$ of rank $[\kappa(D):\kappa(V)]$, with no Noetherian, finiteness or completeness assumption on $D$ itself. It is used by [`Algebra.Etale.quotient_tensorProduct_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_isSeparable`](thm.html#Algebra.Etale.quotient_tensorProduct_of_flat_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_of_isSeparable) in the study of flat local algebras with separable residue extension.
